{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016EGnTLtRW8CmAnib2kSCA6","type":"tool_result","content":"   320→\n   321→## [0.4.1] - 2026-02-13\n   322→\n   323→...\n   324→```\n   325→\n   326→Rules:\n   327→\n   328→- Always have an `[Unreleased]` section at the top\n   329→- Entries use **bold name** — description format\n   330→- Group entries under Added/Changed/Fixed subsections\n   331→- The release script stamps [Unreleased] → [version] - date automatically\n   332→- Entries are assembled during PR work, cleaned up at release time\n   333→- If a version wasn't synced to public, it can be consolidated (e.g., v0.4.0 content was rolled into v0.4.1 because v0.4.0 was internal-only)\n   334→\n   335→---\n   336→\n   337→## 9. Key Files Reference\n   338→\n   339→| File                                   | Purpose                                                                       |\n   340→| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n   341→| `server/index.ts`                      | CLI entry point — arg parsing, routing to commands                            |\n   342→| `server/hankweave-runtime.ts`          | Core runtime — codon execution, state management, event emission              |\n   343→| `server/config.ts`                     | 5-layer config resolution (defaults → hankweave.json → hank.json → env → CLI) |\n   344→| `server/basic-tui.ts`                  | Built-in terminal UI (WebSocket client)                                       |\n   345→| `server/codon-runner.ts`               | Runs individual codons via harness managers                                   |\n   346→| `server/claude-agent-sdk-manager.ts`   | Claude Code SDK integration                                                   |\n   347→| `server/shim-process-manager.ts`       | Process manager for shim-based harnesses (Codex, Gemini)                      |\n   348→| `server/remote-hank.ts`                | Git-based remote hank fetching and caching                                    |\n   349→| `server/sentinels/`                    | Sentinel system (event-triggered observers)                                   |\n   350→| `server/telemetry/`                    | Anonymous usage telemetry (PostHog)                                           |\n   351→| `server/schemas/event-schemas.ts`      | WebSocket event type definitions (Zod)                                        |\n   352→| `server/config-validation/`            | Validation schemas for hank files and configs                                 |\n   353→| `tests/utils/sentinel-test-harness.ts` | Shared test utilities for sentinel tests                                      |\n   354→| `tests/utils/mock-llm.ts`              | Mock LLM provider for integration tests                                       |\n   355→\n   356→---\n   357→\n   358→## 10. Environment & Secrets\n   359→\n   360→### Local development\n   361→\n   362→No secrets needed for unit/integration tests. E2E tests need:\n   363→\n   364→- `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` — Claude Code access\n   365→- `GEMINI_API_KEY` — Gemini CLI access\n   366→- `HANKWEAVE_SENTINEL_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` — for sentinel LLM calls\n   367→- Codex auth via `~/.codex/auth.json`\n   368→\n   369→### CI secrets\n   370→\n   371→Same as above, plus:\n   372→\n   373→- `NPM_TOKEN` — for npm publish\n   374→- `CODEX_AUTH_JSON` — Codex authentication JSON\n   375→- `PUBLIC_REPO_PAT` — GitHub PAT for pushing to the public repo during sync\n   376→\n   377→---\n   378→\n   379→## 11. AI Agent Policy\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10b5aa3-09ea-414c-b37c-8b03ba239eca","uuid":"a52cb810-350c-4914-b26f-93eec1ee7e9d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/source/hankweave/standard-operating-procedures.md","content":"\n## [0.4.1] - 2026-02-13\n\n...\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Always have an `[Unreleased]` section at the top\n- Entries use **bold name** — description format\n- Group entries under Added/Changed/Fixed subsections\n- The release script stamps [Unreleased] → [version] - date automatically\n- Entries are assembled during PR work, cleaned up at release time\n- If a version wasn't synced to public, it can be consolidated (e.g., v0.4.0 content was rolled into v0.4.1 because v0.4.0 was internal-only)\n\n---\n\n## 9. Key Files Reference\n\n| File                                   | Purpose                                                                       |\n| -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `server/index.ts`                      | CLI entry point — arg parsing, routing to commands                            |\n| `server/hankweave-runtime.ts`          | Core runtime — codon execution, state management, event emission              |\n| `server/config.ts`                     | 5-layer config resolution (defaults → hankweave.json → hank.json → env → CLI) |\n| `server/basic-tui.ts`                  | Built-in terminal UI (WebSocket client)                                       |\n| `server/codon-runner.ts`               | Runs individual codons via harness managers                                   |\n| `server/claude-agent-sdk-manager.ts`   | Claude Code SDK integration                                                   |\n| `server/shim-process-manager.ts`       | Process manager for shim-based harnesses (Codex, Gemini)                      |\n| `server/remote-hank.ts`                | Git-based remote hank fetching and caching                                    |\n| `server/sentinels/`                    | Sentinel system (event-triggered observers)                                   |\n| `server/telemetry/`                    | Anonymous usage telemetry (PostHog)                                           |\n| `server/schemas/event-schemas.ts`      | WebSocket event type definitions (Zod)                                        |\n| `server/config-validation/`            | Validation schemas for hank files and configs                                 |\n| `tests/utils/sentinel-test-harness.ts` | Shared test utilities for sentinel tests                                      |\n| `tests/utils/mock-llm.ts`              | Mock LLM provider for integration tests                                       |\n\n---\n\n## 10. Environment & Secrets\n\n### Local development\n\nNo secrets needed for unit/integration tests. E2E tests need:\n\n- `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` — Claude Code access\n- `GEMINI_API_KEY` — Gemini CLI access\n- `HANKWEAVE_SENTINEL_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` — for sentinel LLM calls\n- Codex auth via `~/.codex/auth.json`\n\n### CI secrets\n\nSame as above, plus:\n\n- `NPM_TOKEN` — for npm publish\n- `CODEX_AUTH_JSON` — Codex authentication JSON\n- `PUBLIC_REPO_PAT` — GitHub PAT for pushing to the public repo during sync\n\n---\n\n## 11. AI Agent Policy","numLines":60,"startLine":320,"totalLines":406}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:19:37.070Z"}
