{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01CVcKFcQFBvwhyPbePGUoeY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018PWMwNdUFb5n35GkVWFKUc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/implementations/current/implementation_issues.md","content":"# Implementation Issues Log\n\nThis document records issues, deviations, and observations discovered during the implementation of the monorepo migration plan (`plan/merged/plan.md`).\n\n---\n\n## Issue 1: Pre-existing typecheck failure unrelated to migration\n\n**Observed during**: Phase 6 verification (Step 6 - `bun run typecheck`).\n\n**Description**: Running `bun run typecheck` (which calls `tsc --noEmit`) fails with:\n\n```\nerror TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for 'bun-types'.\n  The file is in the program because:\n    Entry point of type library 'bun-types' specified in compilerOptions\n```\n\n**Root cause**: The `bun-types` package is stored in `node_modules/.bun/bun-types@1.3.6/node_modules/bun-types/` rather than directly at `node_modules/bun-types/`. This means the TypeScript compiler (`tsc`) cannot find it via normal module resolution. The `@types/bun` package exists at `node_modules/@types/bun/index.d.ts` which is the newer recommended package, but `tsconfig.json` still references `\"types\": [\"bun-types\"]` (the older package name).\n\n**Confirmed pre-existing**: Verified by running `git stash` to revert all migration changes and re-running the typecheck — the identical failure occurs. This is not a regression introduced by the migration.\n\n**Impact on migration**: None. The plan's Phase 6.1 (`bun run tc`) step will surface this failure, but it should be noted as pre-existing in the plan. The plan's claim \"None of these should be affected by the migration\" is accurate.\n\n**Recommended follow-up for plan update**: Add a note in Section g (Testing Considerations) or Section f (Phase 6) that `bun run tc` has a pre-existing failure related to `bun-types` resolution that is unrelated to the monorepo migration. The future implementer should not be alarmed by this failure.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 2: Unit tests have 9 pre-existing failures unrelated to migration\n\n**Observed during**: Phase 6 verification (`bun run test:unit`).\n\n**Description**: 9 unit tests fail consistently with errors like:\n\n```\nerror: Codex binary not found in node_modules. Ensure @openai/codex-sdk is installed.\n```\n\nand several `expect(result).not.toBeNull()` failures in what appear to be Codex locator tests.\n\n**Confirmed pre-existing**: Verified by running `git stash` and re-running the unit tests — the identical 9 failures occur. Total: 1512 pass, 4 skip, 9 fail.\n\n**Impact on migration**: None. These failures are unrelated to the workspace/docs changes.\n\n**Recommended follow-up for plan update**: Add a note in Section g (Testing Considerations) that the test suite has 9 pre-existing failures related to Codex binary resolution. The migration does not affect these tests.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 3: `bun install` regenerates a significantly larger bun.lock\n\n**Observed during**: Phase 1, Step 1.4 (`bun install`).\n\n**Description**: Running `bun install` after adding `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` to `package.json` regenerated `bun.lock` with approximately 1,071 additional lines (from the docs workspace dependencies: `next`, `nextra`, `react`, `posthog-js`, etc.). The final install completed successfully with \"1614 packages installed\" in ~8 seconds.\n\n**Peer dependency note**: The root `package.json` has `\"peerDependencies\": { \"typescript\": \"^5.9.2\" }` and the docs `package.json` has `\"devDependencies\": { \"typescript\": \"^5.0.0\" }`. Bun resolved this without warnings, choosing `typescript@5.9.3`. No peer dependency conflict was observed (the plan anticipated a possible warning; none materialized).\n\n**Impact**: The plan accurately described this step. The lockfile diff is large but expected.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 4: `schemas/hankweave.schema.json` changes after `bun install`\n\n**Observed during**: Post-`bun install` git diff.\n\n**Description**: Running `bun run generate-schemas` after `bun install` modified `schemas/hankweave.schema.json` with 4 lines changed. This is likely because the new `typescript@5.9.3` version resolved from the unified lockfile generated slightly different Zod-to-JSON output.\n\n**Impact**: Minor. The schema diff is cosmetic and captured in the migration commit. This is a one-time artifact of the dependency resolution. Future `generate-schemas` runs will be stable.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 5: The plan recommends `git checkout develop` in Phase 0 but the working directory is already the hankweave repo\n\n**Observed during**: Understanding the workspace layout during implementation.\n\n**Description**: The implementation is being applied directly to the `source/hankweave` directory (which is already the cloned hankweave git repo). Phase 0 in the plan describes creating a feature branch with `git checkout develop && git pull && git checkout -b hrishi/monorepo-migration`. In the actual workflow (as experienced by this agent), the work was done directly on `develop` without creating a feature branch.\n\n**Impact**: The migration changes are currently sitting as uncommitted modifications on `develop`. In a real production scenario, a feature branch should be created as Phase 0 describes. The plan is correct - the implementation deviated from it.\n\n**Recommended follow-up for plan update**: This is not a plan error, just a note about the actual execution context. The plan's Phase 0 remains correct for the real implementation scenario.\n\n---\n\n## Issue 6: `docs/bun.lock` was in nextra-site and needed to be deleted before `bun install`\n\n**Observed during**: Phase 1, Steps 1.1-1.4.\n\n**Description**: When copying `nextra-site/*` into `docs/`, the copy included `nextra-site/bun.lock`. The plan correctly identifies this in Step 1.3: \"Delete the docs-side `bun.lock`\". This was done with a plain `rm docs/bun.lock` before running `bun install`. Since the file had not yet been git-committed, `git rm` was not needed.\n\n**Impact**: None — the plan handled this correctly. Worth confirming the implementation followed the plan's precise sequence.\n\n---\n\n## Overall Assessment\n\nThe implementation matched the plan closely. All 8 phases were executed successfully:\n\n1. `docs/` directory created with nextra-site contents (minus `bun.lock`)\n2. `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` added to root `package.json`\n3. `tsconfig.json` updated with `\"docs/**/*\"` in `exclude`\n4. `generate-schemas.ts` path updated to use `docs/public/schemas/`\n5. `sync-public.ts` updated: `STRIP_DIRS` + `delete pkg.workspaces`\n6. `release.ts` updated: `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` + schema diff/revert/add\n7. `test-sync-local.ts` updated: rsync `--exclude='docs'` + `shouldNotExist` list\n8. `.gitignore` updated with docs build artifacts\n9. `standard-operating-procedures.md` updated across all four sections\n\nVerification:\n- `bun install`: success, 1614 packages, unified lockfile generated\n- `bun run lint:fix`: clean (230 files, no fixes needed)\n- `bun run generate-schemas`: success, schemas written to both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`\n- `npm pack --dry-run`: `docs/` correctly excluded from tarball\n- Unit tests: 1512 pass / 4 skip / 9 fail (9 failures pre-existing, not related to migration)\n- Typecheck: pre-existing `bun-types` resolution failure (not related to migration)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":86614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483},"output_tokens":2018,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a10b5aa3-09ea-414c-b37c-8b03ba239eca","uuid":"3c157f32-a2c4-4701-9c61-69090f6bf485","timestamp":"2026-03-05T13:30:12.541Z"}
